d by the data, showing a small but statistically significant positive association between dark skin tone and red card probability", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis", "conclusion"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 9, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[11, 12]], "note": "blank line + section divider"}, {"id": 10, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[13, 14]], "note": "section heading: Primary Estimand"}, {"id": 11, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[15, 16]], "note": "restates definition of the adjusted risk difference estimand"}, {"id": 12, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[17, 18]], "note": "Results label"}, {"id": 13, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[19, 21]], "assertion": "the adjusted risk difference is +0.278 percentage points, 95% CI [0.047,0.537], two-sided p=0.0215", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 14, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[22, 22]], "assertion": "after adjusting for games, yellow cards, goals, position, and league country, dark-skinned players have an estimated 0.28 percentage point higher probability of a red card", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted risk difference", "confounders"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [15]}, {"id": 15, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[22, 22]], "assertion": "this 0.28pp difference represents a 23% relative increase over the baseline risk of 1.22% for light-skinned players", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["relative increase", "baseline risk"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [14]}, {"id": 16, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[23, 24]], "note": "Methodological Notes label"}, {"id": 17, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[25, 25]], "assertion": "the risk difference was calculated using marginal standardization (g-computation)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["risk difference", "marginal standardization"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 18, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[26, 26]], "assertion": "predictions were made for the entire sample under both exposure conditions", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["predictions", "exposure conditions"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 19, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[27, 27]], "assertion": "the standard error and CI were derived from a parametric bootstrap (1,000 simulations) based on the model coefficients' variance-covariance matrix", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["standard error", "confidence interval", "parametric bootstrap"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 20, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[28, 28]], "assertion": "the p-value came from a GEE model Wald test", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["p-value", "Wald test"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 21, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[29, 30]], "note": "blank line + section divider"}, {"id": 22, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[31, 32]], "note": "section heading: Secondary Estimand"}, {"id": 23, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[33, 34]], "note": "Results label"}, {"id": 24, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[35, 36]], "assertion": "the adjusted odds ratio is 1.239, 95% CI [1.032,1.486]", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 25, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[37, 37]], "assertion": "odds of a red card are 24% higher for dark-skinned players holding covariates constant", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["odds ratio interpretation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 26, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[38, 39]], "note": "blank line + section divider"}, {"id": 27, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[40, 41]], "note": "section heading: Model and Estimation Details"}, {"id": 28, "kind": "nonclaim", "subty