ction is positive (dark>light), consistent with the hypothesis", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect direction"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 101, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[139, 139]], "assertion": "the magnitude of +0.28pp is small absolutely but a 23% relative increase over baseline", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect magnitude"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 102, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[140, 140]], "assertion": "statistical significance is p=0.022, below the α=0.05 threshold", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["statistical significance"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 103, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[141, 141]], "assertion": "the 95% CI [0.05,0.54] excludes zero, indicating the true effect likely lies in that range", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confidence interval", "precision"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 104, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[142, 142]], "assertion": "the effect is consistent across both the risk difference and odds ratio metrics", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness", "risk difference", "odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 105, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[143, 143]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 106, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[144, 144]], "note": "subsection heading: Practical Significance"}, {"id": 107, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[145, 145]], "note": "lead-in framing statement"}, {"id": 108, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[146, 148]], "assertion": "baseline risk for light skin is 1.22%, risk for dark skin is 1.50%, a 23% relative increase", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["baseline risk", "relative increase"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 109, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[149, 149]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 110, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[150, 150]], "assertion": "given the serious consequences of red cards, even a modest risk increase represents a tangible disadvantage for dark-skinned players", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["practical significance"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 111, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[151, 151]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 112, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[152, 152]], "note": "subsection heading: Comparison to Unadjusted Analysis"}, {"id": 113, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[153, 154]], "assertion": "the unadjusted risk difference was +0.20pp versus an adjusted risk difference of +0.28pp", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["unadjusted risk difference", "adjusted risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 114, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[155, 155]], "assertion": "adjusting for confounders increased the estimated effect, suggesting confounding had been masking part of the association", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confounding adjustment"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 115, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[156, 156]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 116, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[157, 157]], "assertion": "the pattern arose because dark-skinned players are more common in higher-card leagues (France, England) but more often play forward (lower-card) positions, so adjusting reveals a larger skin-tone effect", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confounding explanation", "league", "position"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 117, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[158, 158]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 118, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[159, 159]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 119, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[160, 160]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 120, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[161, 161]], "note": "section heading: 